{
  "opening": "This release focuses on stabilizing core caching behaviors and introducing new eviction strategies to complement the existing LRU and TTL implementations. We must ensure that exception handling in `popitem` is robust, that key pickling works reliably across all cache types, and that the new FIFO and MRU caches are exposed with their correct public names.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "Cache keys must be correctly serialized and deserialized via pickle for all supported cache classes, ensuring no data corruption or loss of state upon unpickling."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "When `popitem` raises an exception due to an empty cache, the exception context must clearly indicate the cause without obscuring the original traceback information."
    },
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "The library must expose a new `MRUCache` class that implements the Most Recently Used eviction algorithm, accessible as `cachetools.MRUCache`, alongside the `mru_cache` decorator."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "The library must expose a new `FIFOCache` class that implements the First-In-First-Out eviction algorithm, accessible as `cachetools.FIFOCache`, alongside the `fifo_cache` decorator."
    },
    {
      "id": "m32",
      "text": "Implementations of `LFUCache`, `LRUCache`, and `MRUCache` must ensure that items added by a custom `__missing__` method are properly stored in the cache and counted towards the size limit."
    },
    {
      "id": "m60",
      "text": "The expiration time for entries in `TTLCache` must be calculated precisely based on the current time at insertion, ensuring consistent and predictable timeout behavior."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that these changes integrate smoothly with the existing decorator ecosystem and maintain backward compatibility for users relying on standard cache operations."
}
